          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4bcfe1e16a0c77e17ede39093922ba351a73242228f41a40d354058ec91f7d48:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e544c7b799d34517b1524887d52fc6ab",
      "statement": "When response_format is configured, create_agent handles three strategies: ProviderStrategy (uses model's native API), ToolStrategy (creates pseudo-tools for schema), and AutoStrategy (auto-detects based on model capabilities). ToolStrategy adds structured tools to the model's tool list, and the agent automatically routes to termination after a structured tool is called instead of looping.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L1246-L1349",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:246c9265deed710d91da5adb6b5465cd1c5f7db5eac35956c7b5380908019280:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L1407-L1441",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9d23a6c1d65a89fbb906189ff309e59258a7b3b6b5c146f6a4459cce13d1e6f5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dbd78fdd511646248d0f11f43bc955f2",
      "statement": "Node hooks (before_model, after_model, before_agent, after_agent) can return dict state updates or None. Middleware hooks can set state['jump_to'] to: 'model' (loop back), 'tools' (execute tools), or 'end' (terminate), allowing explicit control over the agent flow independent of tool call decisions.",
      "evidence": [
        {
